<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="world-drops">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/expansionicon_mistsofpandaria.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best World Drop Items for Balance Druid</span></h2>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="the-celestial-court">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_pet_tigergodcub.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> The Celestial Court</span></h3>Chi-ji, Yu'Lon, Xuen, and Niuzao all share a loot pool and drop item level 553 Tier 16. In addition, these can drop a variety of Season 14 PvP pieces, although the tier set is by far the most valuable loot. These are also quite easy compared to previous world bosses, and will be killed quite frequently due to everyone needing to kill them for the Legendary cloak questline, so make sure you don't miss a kill every week!<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="ordos">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_axe_1h_firelandsraid_d_02.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Ordos, Fire God of the Yaungol</span></h3>Ordos drops some decent pieces, such as <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105764/rising-new-moon-talisman">
<img alt="Rising New Moon Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_necklace_mop5.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rising New Moon Talisman</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105770/zoo-pers-superior-chestguard">
<img alt="Zoo-Per's Superior Chestguard" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_leather_raiddruid_n_01pant.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zoo-Per's Superior Chestguard</span></a>. These are fairly rare, but are all higher item level than the celestial pieces, making them good alternatives despite the weaker stats and lack of strong sockets<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="world-drops-2">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_staff_2h_pandarenmonk_c_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Timeless Isle Items for Balance Druid</span></h2>The Timeless Isle in Phase 5 is great for catching up on gear.  You will earn <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/currency=777/timeless-coin">
<span>
<img alt="Timeless Coin" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/timelesscoin.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Timeless Coin</span></span></a> for almost all activities that you participate in.  <br/>
<br/>There are several good pieces of catch-up gear from the isle. Most notable is the new trinket, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=103987/yulons-bite">
<img alt="Yu'lon's Bite" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_jadeserpentpet.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Yu'lon's Bite</span></a>, which requires a hefty 50,000 <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/currency=777/timeless-coin">
<span>
<img alt="Timeless Coin" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/timelesscoin.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Timeless Coin</span></span></a>, although it is worse than the two celestial trinkets available. Otherwise, you can find a variety of 496 items scattered around the isle, and use the rare drop <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=103982/burden-of-eternity">
<img alt="Burden of Eternity" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_monk_envelopingmist.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Burden of Eternity</span></a> to upgrade them to 535 item level.<br/>[/<wbr/>b][/<wbr/>center] [/<wbr/>div] [/<wbr/>grid]<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_offhand_ulduarraid_d_03.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Balance Druid Pre-Raid Trinkets in Phase 5</span></h2>
<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>Balance Druid should typically use two passive trinkets, and sometimes one on-use and one passive, but rarely ever two on-use. In the case of Phase 4 of Mists of Pandaria, we will default to our two standard passive trinkets.<br/>
<br/>
<ins>Active Trinkets</ins>
<br/>There are no active trinkets of note worth mentioning for Balance Druid, as all of our strongest trinkets are Passive Trinkets.<br/>
<br/>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105422/purified-bindings-of-immerseus">
<img alt="Purified Bindings of Immerseus" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Purified Bindings of Immerseus</span></a> is by far our best option for a trinket in T16. Not only does it have a high intellect proc, but the amplification effect is also very strong considering the amount of stats we possess in T16. There is no better trinket for the rest of the game.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105540/kardris-toxic-totem">
<img alt="Kardris' Toxic Totem" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Kardris' Toxic Totem</span></a> also comes with a strong proc as well as a new unique effect, causing our attacks to sometimes perform "Multistrike". While this effect is only about 4% of our damage, it is enough to push it into second place as our trinket of choice.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105648/black-blood-of-yshaarj">
<img alt="Black Blood of Y'Shaarj" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Black Blood of Y'Shaarj</span></a>is another strong trinket, but lacks the bonus effect seen on our other two best options. It can also be somewhat difficult to fully optimize, as the ramping buff relies on us snapshotting DoTs towards the end of the spell.[/<wbr/>color]</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105572/frenzied-crystal-of-rage">
<img alt="Frenzied Crystal of Rage" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frenzied Crystal of Rage</span></a> is our final option, and while it can perform well on stacked AoE the low proc chance and lack of other strong effects make it slightly worse than the best two options.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="legendary-cloak">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_legendary_theblackprince.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Legendary Cloak for Balance Druid</span></h2>With the removal of Raid Finder in Mists of Pandaria Classic, it is possible to earn your Legendary Cloak without ever setting foot into a raid.  This can be done inside Celestial Dungeons.  <br/>
<br/>In Phase 5, you can at last finish the Legendary Quest Line and earn your Legendary Cloak. For a Balance Druid, our cloak of choice is <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102246/xing-ho-breath-of-yulon">
<img alt="Xing-Ho, Breath of Yu'lon" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_dragoncaster_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Xing-Ho, Breath of Yu'lon</span></a>, which comes with a variety of powerful stats, as well as a strong proc effect that deals a respectable amount of damage, especially in AoE. <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=146197/essence-of-yulon">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/monk_stance_wiseserpent.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Essence of Yu'lon</span></a> can also proc your trinkets, helping us to get early procs in the fight instead of waiting for them!<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="reputation">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/achievement_faction_shadopan_assault.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Reputation Items for Balance Druids</span></h2>
