<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted &amp; Profession Gear for Balance Druids</span></h2>Crafted items are no longer restricted by profession, meaning that even if you aren't a Leatherworker, you can equip anything Leatherworkers craft. There are two crafted items in Tier 15 that we will be looking at. Both require <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94289/haunting-spirit">
<img alt="Haunting Spirit" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_rogue_envelopingshadows.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haunting Spirit</span></a>, which can only be obtained from disenchanting raid loot, which can result in them being very expensive.<br/>
<br/>The following crafted items are all workable up til you have access to better gear from Heroic Siege of Orgrimmar and should be used if you either have an excess of materials or gold to spend at the Auction House.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=98600/pennyroyal-leggings">
<img alt="Pennyroyal Leggings" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pant_leather_panprog_b_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Pennyroyal Leggings</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=98609/pennyroyal-belt">
<img alt="Pennyroyal Belt" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_leather_panprog_b_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Pennyroyal Belt</span></a></div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Balance Druids</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria our Hit cap is 15%. Spirit still converts to Hit for us, and now Expertise also contributes to our Hit cap. At 15% Hit, our spells will no longer miss raid bosses. This requires a total combined Spirit, Hit and Expertise of 5100. Normally we will have no Expertise, although we sometimes have a small amount of it from gems. Reaching Hit cap is very important for us, both because of it being an efficient way to get DPS and because it makes the rotation more predictable.<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Gems for Balance Druids</span></h3>Gems are a great place to grab any Hit that we may be missing. This can be especially useful when aiming for Socket Bonuses, as <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76651/energized-wild-jade">
<img alt="Energized Wild Jade" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_green.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Energized Wild Jade</span></a> and <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76686/purified-imperial-amethyst">
<img alt="Purified Imperial Amethyst" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_purple.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Purified Imperial Amethyst</span></a> are the only good ways to utilize a Blue Socket if we want the bonus.<br/>
<br/>You will generally aim to fill all Blue Sockets then use reforging to ensure Hit cap. If you're still under Hit cap afterwards, then using <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76651/energized-wild-jade">
<img alt="Energized Wild Jade" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_green.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Energized Wild Jade</span></a> in Yellow Sockets is also an option.<br/>
<br/>Once you're at 5100 Hit Rating, things become complex. The general rule of thumb is to prioritize Intellect while grabbing Haste in Yellow Sockets if you are below 5273 Haste rating, without Tier 14 4-piece bonus. If you have Tier 14 4-piece bonus <i>or</i> above 5273 Haste rating, you will instead aim to grab Critical Strike rating from Yellow Sockets.<br/>
<br/>There will also be situations where using pure Haste or Critical Strike gems is better than Intellect gems. This can not be determined without a sim, and so for the best results, it is recommended to always sim yourself.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="q9">Meta Gem</span>: <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95347/sinister-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Sinister Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sinister Primal Diamond</span></a>. Use <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76885/burning-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Burning Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_metagem_cut.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Burning Primal Diamond</span></a> until you have Sinister Primal DIamond.</div></li>
<li>
